From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexbob0 <alex@kerfystudio.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 13:59:31 +0100
Subject: Prompt cache: the Bot Chat section last, memory the day's copy with a
 turn note, run instructions as a turn note

The Bot Mode section moves to the volatile tier, after the memory and the profile line, so a Bot Chat shares its
prompt with the agent's other conversations up to there. With memory.prompt_refresh: daily (the default for agents)
the memory blocks are the day's copy (memories/.prompt-day.json, taken by the day's first load); what is written
later is told in a turn note (added and removed entries against the prompt, sent when that difference changes).
On api_server the run's instructions leave the system prompt for a turn note, sent when they change.

BipAgents patch, documented in hermes/patches/README.md of the BipAgents repository.

Bip-Patch: 0023-prompt-cache-stable-across-conversations
